course: dictionary
lesson: 15885
title: Unintended
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some things happen even though nobody meant them to. The word unintended means not planned or not meant to happen. The prefix un- means not, and intend means to plan or mean to do something, so unintended means not intended.
explain: «The loud bang was unintended; the football hit the window by accident.» Nobody wanted the window to break, so the breaking was unintended. When you meet this word, ask yourself: did someone plan this? If not, unintended may fit.
explain: Scientists and historians use this word too. «The new medicine had an unintended effect: it made some people sleepy.» The makers did not want sleepiness. It was a side effect they did not plan, so it was unintended.
fact: Unintended means not planned or not meant to happen.
fact: The prefix un- means not, so unintended means not intended.
fact: Unintended can describe a result, an effect, harm, or a consequence.
fact: An unintended consequence is an effect that nobody planned.
fact: Unintended is an adjective, so it describes a noun, as in «an unintended result».
exercise: «The spilled paint was unintended; Sam only meant to tidy the desk.» What does unintended mean here? | Planned very carefully | *Not planned | Loud and colourful | Done again and again
exercise: The new road made traffic worse for the village, an unintended result of the plan. What does unintended suggest? | The traffic was a planned surprise | The village asked for more traffic | *Nobody meant this to happen | The road was the goal of the plan
exercise: Which word means the same as unintended? | careful | loud | *accidental | planned
test: «Her kind words had an unintended effect: they made her brother cry.» Did she plan to make him cry? | Yes, it was her plan all along | *No, it was not meant to happen | Yes, she wanted him to laugh | No, she was too ill to speak
test: Which is an unintended consequence? | A walk planned for Sunday morning | A new park built by the council after a vote | A cake baked for a birthday party | *A forest fire started by a dropped match that nobody wanted
exam: What is the best meaning of unintended? | Planned with great care | Very old and famous | *Not planned or not meant to happen | Happy and surprised by a gift
